course: dictionary
lesson: 9599
title: Old words with a story
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words are very old, and people still use them today. «Others, like "blimey" and "strewth", were once oaths about God that have worn soft with time.» An oath is a serious promise or a swear word. Over time, people stopped meaning the God part and kept the word as a gentle sound of surprise.
explain: «"Strewth!" is an Australian cry of surprise that comes from "God's truth".» Read the words around strewth to find its job. If someone drops their ice cream and says «Strewth!», they are surprised or a little annoyed, not angry. The word is mild, so it is safe for a classroom.
explain: Strewth is also written as struth. Older people in Australia and in old British speech use it most, and films about Australians often use it for comic effect. When you meet a word like this, a dictionary tells you where it comes from and who uses it.
fact: An exclamation is a short word or cry that shows a strong feeling, like surprise.
fact: «Strewth» means a mild exclamation of surprise, shock or annoyance.
fact: «Strewth» comes from "God's truth", but it is not used to talk about God now.
fact: «Strewth» is old-fashioned and is mostly used in Australia and New Zealand, and by older people.
fact: Its other spelling is «struth», and both spellings mean the same thing.
exercise: «Strewth!» is an Australian cry of surprise. What is it? | A loud sneeze | A type of Australian food | *A mild cry of surprise | A name for a kind of bird
exercise: Where does «strewth» come from? | From the word struggle | From an old song about rain | *From "God's truth" | A ship's name
exercise: Which people often say «strewth», according to the lessons? | Only sailors | *Older people in Australia and old British speech | Scientists in laboratories | Only people in films
test: Dad drops his toast and says «Strewth!». What is he feeling? | Very happy | Sleepy | Hungry | *Mild surprise or annoyance
test: Why is «strewth» called an old-fashioned word? | It is a new word from a computer game | It means a long river in Australia | Everyone uses it today in exactly the same way | *It is old speech that came from an oath about God and has worn soft with time
exam: Which sentence shows «strewth» used as a mild exclamation? | Add «strewth» and «two» to get the answer. | *«Strewth, I didn't expect that!» | «Strewth» is the name of a dog in my street. | «Strewth» means a long walk to the shops.
